# Lab 20: Replay one failed notebook registration POST
#
# The tracked version contains placeholders and must not be sent.
# Do not paste private values into the tracked version.
# Follow ../INSTRUCTION.md, "Replay a failed notebook POST in REST Client", to
# export the captured request into the ignored evidence directory.
#
# The exported copy contains the original bearer token and real identifiers.
# Do not commit, share, screenshot, or copy it outside protected local evidence.
#
# Exporting does not send a request or resolve the notebook's pending write.
# REST Client does not enforce the notebook's pending_write guard.
# Before sending, reconcile the earlier outcome or obtain explicit approval
# for one disposable replay acknowledging that a 500 can still hide a write.
# Do not remove the pending marker merely to retry.
#
# Preserve the captured body, including both identity fields and source ID.
# Use the captured token while valid. A refreshed token changes the auth
# context and must be recorded as a separate experiment condition.
#
# Send once only. Save status and response privately, including any returned ID.
# A 201 requires readback and reconciliation before resuming the notebook.
# Another 500 is not evidence of no write; stop rather than sending again.
# Keep the local working copy during the approved diagnostic sequence.
# When finished, remove its bearer value or delete the private working copy.

# @name replayNotebookRegistration
POST https://graph.microsoft.com/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations
Authorization: {{capturedAuthorization}}
Content-Type: {{capturedContentType}}
Accept: {{capturedAccept}}
OData-Version: {{capturedODataVersion}}

{{capturedRequestBody}}
